Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:08:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): retain lexical redirection provenance through
 quote removal [daveey]

Quote-stripped argv was misclassified as real descriptor close/rebind syntax, erasing known stdin sources. Carry parsed redirection metadata beside decoded words, protecting literal punctuation and escaping the encoding character itself. Preserve descriptor transfers and target filenames.

Proof: all four reported malicious stdin regressions fail on 9e7dcd953c and pass with repair; harmless real Bash markers and benign scripts pass. Full lifecycle consumer run: 3207 passed before added collision controls; final-head consumers rerun after canonical publication. Adds quote-fragment sentinel collision controls with dangerous/benign files swapped. Review 5901419054 repair; landing owner t_01a1d756e3461c64 retains independent final-head review and merge.
